<title>UK: Commerzbank sets 2.5 bln Lux franc step-up bond.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank sets 2.5 bln Lux franc step-up bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated step-up bond was announced by joint lead managers Credit Europeen and Banque Bruxelles Lambert SA.</p>
<p> BORROWER   COMMERZBANK</p>
<p> AMT    2.5 BLN LUF   COUPON    *6.0	 MATURITY    15.DEC.06</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  102.65  L PAY DATE 14/15.NOV.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 YIELD	6.61 PCT  L LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY    **AA3	 LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K)  50-250</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    =	   SELL CONC  =	   PRAECIPUUM  0.25</p>
<p> NOTES     *FOR YEARS ONE TO FOUR, 7.0 PCT IN YEARS FIVE TO</p>
<p>		SEVEN AND 9.0 PCT THEREAFTER.</p>
<p>	    **THE SUBORDINATED RATING.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF AN MTN PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
